`E″` of the fiber is `2`-isogenous to the pair curve of `(p, q) = (2UV, W²) = (54264, 133225)`
(`IsPerfectCuboid.not_onFiber_of_isogeny`), with `D = q² − p² = (U² − V²)² = 14804318929`. The
descent for this pair has 6400 groups `(λ, σ₀)` over 576 values of `λ`; 6368 of them
are ruled out by their `2`-descent class (`ClassKill`, with 504 distinct class tests), and
the other 19852 cases are split out, 13132 of them torsion translates. The kernel
replays the certificate with `classCert` (`decide +kernel`).

The curve `E″` has rank `0` and its `2`-Selmer group is its torsion modulo `2` (PARI/GP); this is
only the reason to expect the descent to work, and the proofs do not depend on it.

